{
  "slug": "artist:kendrick-lamar",
  "name": "Kendrick Lamar",
  "editorial_article": "Born in Compton, California, on June 17, 1987, Kendrick Lamar Duckworth debuted his commercial career after signing with Top Dawg Entertainment in 2005. His breakthrough arrived with his 2012 sophomore project, Good Kid, M.A.A.D City, which utilized producers such as Pharrell Williams and Hit-Boy to craft a narrative-driven gangsta rap record. By 2015, Lamar reached number one on the Billboard 200 with To Pimp a Butterfly, an album that integrated jazz, funk, and soul influences with the help of collaborators like Thundercat and Terrace Martin. In 2018, he became the first rapper to win the Pulitzer Prize for Music. Beyond his solo work, Lamar co-founded the creative company PGLang and famously engaged in a public musical feud with Drake that culminated in 2024's chart-topping singles like 'Not Like Us'.",
